{"name":"Manticore Brown","hex":"#957840","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"manticore","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A beast with the body of a lion (usually red), the tail of a scorpion, and the head/face of a man with a mouth filled with multiple rows of sharp teeth (like a shark), said to be able to shoot spikes from its tail or mane to paralyse prey. It may be horned, winged, or both; its voice is described as a mixture of pipes and trumpets."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manticore"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Manticore","blocks":[{"text":"The manticore or mantichore is a legendary creature from ancient Persian mythology, similar to the Egyptian sphinx that also proliferated in Western European medieval art. It has the face of a human, the body of a lion, and the tail of a scorpion or a tail covered in venomous spines similar to porcupine quills. There are some accounts that the spines can be launched like arrows. It eats its victims whole, using its three rows of teeth, and leaves no bones behind."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Martigora_ca_1652_%2821203315%29.jpg/330px-Martigora_ca_1652_%2821203315%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manticore","wikidata":"Q223795"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso